{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Embeddings & Vector Representations Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We build a semantic search engine from scratch. No vector database. No external embedding API. Pure Python with numpy for the math."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Text Chunking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_text(text, chunk_size=200, overlap=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    words = text.split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    start = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while start < len(words):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        end = start + chunk_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunk = \" \".join(words[start:end])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks.append(chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start += chunk_size - overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return chunks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_by_sentences(text, max_chunk_tokens=200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sentences = text.replace(\"\\n\", \" \").split(\".\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sentences = [s.strip() + \".\" for s in sentences if s.strip()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    current_chunk = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    current_length = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sentence in sentences:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sentence_length = len(sentence.split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if current_length + sentence_length > max_chunk_tokens and current_chunk:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunks.append(\" \".join(current_chunk))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            current_chunk = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            current_length = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        current_chunk.append(sentence)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        current_length += sentence_length"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if current_chunk:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks.append(\" \".join(current_chunk))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return chunks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Building Embeddings from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We implement a simple dense embedding using TF-IDF with L2 normalization. This is not a neural embedding, but it follows the same contract: text in, fixed-size vector out, similar texts produce similar vectors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SimpleEmbedder:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vocab = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.idf = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.word_to_idx = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, documents):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vocab_set = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for doc in documents:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            vocab_set.update(doc.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vocab = sorted(vocab_set)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.word_to_idx = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(self.vocab)}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(documents)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.idf = np.zeros(len(self.vocab))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, word in enumerate(self.vocab):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            doc_count = sum(1 for doc in documents if word in doc.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.idf[i] = math.log((n + 1) / (doc_count + 1)) + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def embed(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        words = text.lower().split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        count = Counter(words)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total = len(words) if words else 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vec = np.zeros(len(self.vocab))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for word, freq in count.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if word in self.word_to_idx:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tf = freq / total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                vec[self.word_to_idx[word]] = tf * self.idf[self.word_to_idx[word]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        norm = np.linalg.norm(vec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if norm > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            vec = vec / norm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return vec"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Similarity Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine_similarity(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = np.dot(a, b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_a = np.linalg.norm(a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_b = np.linalg.norm(b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if norm_a == 0 or norm_b == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return float(dot / (norm_a * norm_b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def dot_product(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return float(np.dot(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def euclidean_distance(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return float(np.linalg.norm(a - b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Vector Index with Brute-Force Search"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class VectorIndex:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vectors = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.texts = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.metadata = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def add(self, vector, text, meta=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vectors.append(vector)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.texts.append(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.metadata.append(meta or {})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def search(self, query_vector, top_k=5, metric=\"cosine\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, vec in enumerate(self.vectors):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if metric == \"cosine\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score = cosine_similarity(query_vector, vec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            elif metric == \"dot\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score = dot_product(query_vector, vec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            elif metric == \"euclidean\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score = -euclidean_distance(query_vector, vec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                raise ValueError(f\"Unknown metric: {metric}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            scores.append((i, score))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        results = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx, score in scores[:top_k]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            results.append({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"text\": self.texts[idx],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"score\": score,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"metadata\": self.metadata[idx],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"index\": idx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            })"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def size(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(self.vectors)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: The Semantic Search Engine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SemanticSearchEngine:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, chunk_size=200, overlap=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embedder = SimpleEmbedder()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.index = VectorIndex()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.chunk_size = chunk_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.overlap = overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def index_documents(self, documents, source_names=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        all_chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        all_sources = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, doc in enumerate(documents):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunks = chunk_text(doc, self.chunk_size, self.overlap)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            all_chunks.extend(chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            name = source_names[i] if source_names else f\"doc_{i}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            all_sources.extend([name] * len(chunks))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embedder.fit(all_chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for chunk, source in zip(all_chunks, all_sources):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            vec = self.embedder.embed(chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.index.add(vec, chunk, {\"source\": source})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(all_chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def search(self, query, top_k=5, metric=\"cosine\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        query_vec = self.embedder.embed(query)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.index.search(query_vec, top_k, metric)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def search_with_scores(self, query, top_k=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        results = self.search(query, top_k)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"text\": r[\"text\"][:200],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"source\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"source\", \"unknown\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"score\": round(r[\"score\"], 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for r in results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Comparing Similarity Metrics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compare_metrics(engine, query, top_k=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    results = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for metric in [\"cosine\", \"dot\", \"euclidean\"]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        hits = engine.search(query, top_k=top_k, metric=metric)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        results[metric] = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            {\"score\": round(h[\"score\"], 4), \"preview\": h[\"text\"][:80]}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for h in hits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Metric comparison**: run the same 5 queries against the sample documents using cosine similarity, dot product, and euclidean distance. Record the top-3 results for each. For which queries do the metrics disagree? Why?\n\n2. **Chunk size experiment**: index the sample documents with chunk sizes of 50, 100, 200, and 500 words. For each, run 5 queries and record the top-1 similarity score. Plot the relationship between chunk size and retrieval quality. Find the point where larger chunks start hurting.\n\n3. **Why truncation needs training**: build a SimpleEmbedder that produces 500-d TF-IDF vectors. Compare three truncation strategies at 50, 100, 200, and 500 dimensions: (a) keep the first N dimensions as-is (alphabetically-first vocabulary words, per `fit()`), (b) keep the N dimensions with the highest average IDF weight across your corpus, (c) keep N random dimensions. Measure retrieval recall for each strategy at each size. Predict before you run it: which strategy degrades most gracefully? Strategy (b) should beat (a) and (c) -- but even (b) won't match a real Matryoshka model's degradation curve, because nothing here was trained with the nested-loss objective from \"Matryoshka Embeddings\" above. That gap is the point: reordering dimensions by importance *after* training helps a little; Matryoshka's actual trick is training the model to put importance there in the first place.\n\n4. **Binary quantization**: take the embeddings from the search engine, convert them to binary (1 if positive, 0 if negative), and implement Hamming distance search. Compare the top-10 results against full-precision cosine similarity. Measure the overlap percentage.\n\n5. **Sentence-based chunking**: replace fixed-size chunking with `chunk_by_sentences`. Run the same queries and compare retrieval scores. Does respecting sentence boundaries improve the results?"
      ]
    }
  ],
